  "title": "Erdős Problem #859",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $t\\geq 1$ and let $d_t$ be the density of the set of integers $n\\in\\mathbb{N}$ for which $t$ can be represented as the sum of distinct divisors of $n$.\nDo there exist constants $c_1,c_2>0$ such that $ d_t \\sim \\frac{c_1}{(\\log t)^{c_2}} $ as $t\\to \\infty$?",
